    "analysis": "The Guidelines describe a party that voluntarily decides to restructure and to bear the related costs in exchange for anticipated savings. Here the taxpayer may incur restructuring costs, but the outsourcing also makes it possible for it to procure the products at a saving compared with its own manufacturing costs. Independent parties setting up this kind of outsourcing might not necessarily insist on explicit compensation from the transferee; the Guidelines give the example of a transferor whose anticipated benefits exceed its restructuring costs. This is not a rule that compensation is never due: it is an example of when it may not be required. A further issue is whether, and how, location savings are to be divided between the parties, which Section D.6 of Chapter I and Section E of Part II address.",
